  "body": "The frozen PR967 D word has no endpoint-neutral pair or triple of elementary ADD omissions. A transported rank-one classification reduces 15,470,703 pairs and 28,677,526,461 triples to 193,704 grouped checks. This extends the credited single-omission atlas, with full-column literal replay and independent dense/planted controls. It does not extend the two fixed diagnostic probes to multiple faults or address four omissions.\n\nValidation: Python 3.12 registered replay with source pins and scoped controls; selected-result integrity or baseline bindings and diff checks pass. See the [reproduction instructions, exact sources and remaining questions](https://github.com/woklerx/integer-mult-bounds/blob/83bab0ac63d7297309e769641d176ca3f12b0124/research/r439-three-omission-distance/README.md). No selected source, certificate or kappa changes; no full selected circuit replay is claimed. Prepared by woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, with predecessor attribution retained.\n",
